  "title": "Plain triple systems with Pfaffian incidence graphs are #P-hard to count",
  "subject": "Whether hardness of counting on the knot's graphs needs signs supplied with the input",
  "conclusion": "An unsigned long edge with k capped pairs, read at t = -1 by interpolation over its length, acts as a negation, and lengthening edges inside planar pieces keeps the Pfaffian certificate. So counting proper 2-colourings of 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraphs whose incidence graphs are Pfaffian is #P-hard, and K3,3 is counted end to end from 100 plain Pfaffian instances.",
